---
import Divider from "../../../../components/ui/Divider.astro";
import Layout from "../../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { Code } from "astro-expressive-code/components";

//#region CodeSnippets
const Q1 = `for (let r = 1; r <= 3; r++) {
  for (let c = 1; c <= 4; c++) {
    console.log(r, c);
  }
}`;
const Q4 = `first <- [1, 2, 3]
second <- first
second[1] <- 99

DISPLAY(first[1])`;
//#endregion
---

<Layout>
  <div class="container my-4">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-10">
        <a href="/courses/ap-csp/" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-light mb-3">
          <i class="si-arrow-left"></i> Back
        </a>

        <h1>Question Set 6</h1>

        <h4 class="text-sn-theme">
          Six questions &middot; 11 minutes &middot; cumulative
        </h4>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="mb-5" />

        <section id="objective">
          <h2>What This Is</h2>

          <p>Five exam-style questions covering Activity 1.1 through 1.22, weighted toward <b>nested loops and the start of lists</b>. Two of these are about the difference between counting from 0 and counting from 1.</p>

          <p>
            <b>Set a timer for 11 minutes.</b> Work them out on paper; do not run
            the code. Mark each answer <b>sure</b> or <b>unsure</b>. Guess
            rather than leave a blank &mdash; the AP exam has no penalty for a
            wrong answer.
          </p>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="questions">
          <h2>The Questions</h2>

          <p>
            Four have exactly one correct answer, one asks you to select
            <i>all</i> that apply, and the last is about data or the impact of
            computing rather than about code. <b>Thirteen of the exam's seventy
            questions look like that last one</b>, so it is on every set from
            here on.
          </p>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Question 1</h3>

          <p>How many times does the innermost line run?</p>

          <Code
            code={Q1}
            frame="code"
            lang="javascript"
            title="Question 1"
            showLineNumbers={false}
            class="mb-3"
          />

          <ul>
            <li>(A) <code>3</code></li>
            <li>(B) <code>4</code></li>
            <li>(C) <code>7</code></li>
            <li>(D) <code>12</code></li>
          </ul>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Question 2</h3>

          <p>In exam notation, given <code>aList &larr; [5, 10, 15]</code>, what is <code>aList[1]</code>?</p>

          <ul>
            <li>(A) <code>5</code></li>
            <li>(B) <code>10</code></li>
            <li>(C) <code>15</code></li>
            <li>(D) An error, because indexing starts at 0</li>
          </ul>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Question 3</h3>

          <p>In JavaScript, given <code>let a = [5, 10, 15];</code>, what is <code>a[1]</code>?</p>

          <ul>
            <li>(A) <code>5</code></li>
            <li>(B) <code>10</code></li>
            <li>(C) <code>15</code></li>
            <li>(D) <code>undefined</code></li>
          </ul>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Question 4</h3>

          <p>What does this display?</p>

          <Code
            code={Q4}
            frame="code"
            lang="txt"
            title="Question 4 — exam notation"
            showLineNumbers={false}
            class="mb-3"
          />

          <ul>
            <li>(A) <code>1</code></li>
            <li>(B) <code>99</code></li>
            <li>(C) <code>2</code></li>
            <li>(D) An error</li>
          </ul>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Question 5 &mdash; Select all that apply</h3>

          <p>Which of these are true about lists on the AP exam reference sheet?</p>

          <ul>
            <li>(A) The first element is at index 1</li>
            <li>(B) <code>aList &larr; bList</code> assigns a copy</li>
            <li>(C) An index of 0 causes the program to terminate</li>
            <li>(D) <code>LENGTH(aList)</code> returns the number of elements</li>
            <li>(E) An index past the end returns <code>undefined</code></li>
          </ul>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Question 6 &mdash; Data and Impact</h3>

          <p>A hiring program is trained on the r&eacute;sum&eacute;s of people a company already hired. Where is bias most likely to enter?</p>

          <ul>
            <li>(A) In the training data, which reflects who was hired before</li>
            <li>(B) In the programming language chosen</li>
            <li>(C) In how fast the program runs</li>
            <li>(D) In the number of r&eacute;sum&eacute;s processed</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="submit">
          <h2>Submit</h2>

          <p>
            Six answers, each marked <b>sure</b> or <b>unsure</b>, plus how far
            you got when the timer went off. Worth <b>2 points</b>, graded on
            completion.
          </p>
        </section>

        <h1
          class="text-center mt-5 text-sn-theme border border-primary slow-flash"
        >
          Start the Timer
        </h1>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
